    "answer": {
      "short": "Blanks in order: $(2x-6)$; $2x-6$; $-2x+6$; $\\frac{11}{3}$; $\\frac{11}{3}$; $\\left|-\\frac43\\right|$; $\\frac43$; $0$; $3$; $\\frac{11}{3}$; $\\frac{11}{3}$. Circle valid.",
      "worked": "The two linear cases give\n$$\\begin{align*}x-5&=2x-6\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nand\n$$\\begin{align*}x-5&=-2x+6\\\\3x&=11\\\\x&=\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$, the left side is $4$ and the right side is $-4$, so this candidate is invalid.\n\nAt $x=\\frac{11}{3}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left|\\frac{11}{3}-5\\right|&=\\left|-\\frac43\\right|\\\\\\left|\\frac{11}{3}-5\\right|&=\\frac43,\\end{align*}$$\nwhile\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\left(\\frac{11}{3}\\right)-6&=\\frac{22}{3}-\\frac{18}{3}\\\\2\\left(\\frac{11}{3}\\right)-6&=\\frac43.\\end{align*}$$\nThus this candidate is valid.\n\nAlternatively, a solution must satisfy $2x-6\\geq0$, so $x\\geq3$. Only $\\frac{11}{3}$ satisfies this condition. The solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
